  "question": "Student Management System Requirements Description:\nThis is a student management system. The main features of the system include:\n1. Student Information Management: Includes information such as name, gender, school, department, and major.\n2. Identification Information Management: Includes information such as identification number, name, gender, age, and address. Each student has unique identification information.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0141\nCREATE TABLE `students` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `identification_number` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `school` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `major` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `identification_number` (`identification_number`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `identification_info` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `identification_number` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `identification_number` (`identification_number`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`identification_number`) REFERENCES `students` (`identification_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
